---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Loop from '../components/Loop.astro';
import Window from '../components/Window.astro';
import Copy from '../components/Copy.astro';
import ForMacs from '../components/ForMacs.astro';
import { latestRelease } from '../lib/release';
import editor from '../../../docs/media/editor.png';
import videoEditor from '../../../docs/media/video-editor.png';
import openAnyway from '../../../docs/media/open-anyway.png';

const release = await latestRelease();
const full = '(min-width: 1120px) 1088px, 100vw';
const half = '(min-width: 900px) 540px, 100vw';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>A better <kbd class="key">⌘</kbd><kbd class="key">⇧</kbd><kbd class="key">4</kbd></h1>
      <p class="lede">Shot is a screenshot app that sits in your menu bar. It uses the keys you already know.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button big" href="/download">Download Shot</a>
        <Copy command="brew install lorcanchinnock/tap/shot" />
      </div>
      <ForMacs />
      <p class="meta">Free and open source. Version {release.version}, for macOS 15 or later, on Apple Silicon or Intel. <a href="#install">How to install</a></p>
      <Window>
        <Loop name="hero" label="Pressing ⌘⇧4, adding a note with an arrow to the problem, then pasting the screenshot into a chat" eager />
      </Window>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="say">Let go of the mouse and the screenshot is already copied and saved. A little card shows up in the corner, and you can drag it straight into a message.</h2>
      <Window><Loop name="capture" label="Dragging out an area with the magnifier, then the Quick Access card sliding into the corner and showing its buttons" /></Window>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap pair">
      <div>
        <h2 class="say">Press <kbd class="key">A</kbd> for an arrow, or <kbd class="key">B</kbd> to blur an email address.</h2>
        <Window><Image src={editor} alt="The annotation editor with a blurred email address, the discount line highlighted, and a sticky note with an arrow pointing at it" widths={[540, 1080]} sizes={half} /></Window>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="say"><kbd class="key">⌘</kbd><kbd class="key">⇧</kbd><kbd class="key">5</kbd> records instead.</h2>
        <Window><Loop name="recording" label="Recording an area of the screen while a chart animates" /></Window>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="say">Then cut the part where you went looking for the right tab, and save it as a GIF.</h2>
      <Window><Image src={videoEditor} alt="The video editor with a trimmed start, a cut where the recording went to another page, a Best day label and an arrow, and the GIF export options" widths={[640, 1088, 1600]} sizes={full} /></Window>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="small">
    <div class="wrap narrow-text">
      <h2 class="say">Circle the bug, and your coding agent sees exactly what you marked. Or let it ask Shot for your latest screenshot, or the key frames of a recording and what you said over them.</h2>
      <p>For your marks to reach the agent, turn on <b>Hand captures to agents</b> in <b>Settings › Agents</b>. The <a href="/docs/#using-shot-with-ai-agents">guide</a> shows how to connect your agent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="small">
    <div class="wrap narrow-text">
      <p>There's no account to make. Shot only goes online to check for updates, and it asks you first. The <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/shot">code is on GitHub</a> if you want to look. Shot is free. If it saves you time, you can <a href="/sponsor">sponsor it</a>.</p>
      <p>Shot speaks English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Brazilian Portuguese, Japanese, Korean and Simplified Chinese, and follows the language your Mac is set to. It follows your Mac's light or dark appearance too, or you can pick one in <b>Settings › General</b>.</p>
      <p>Everything else is in the <a href="/docs/">guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install" id="install">
    <div class="wrap pair">
      <div>
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <Copy command="brew install lorcanchinnock/tap/shot" />
        <p>Or <a href="/download">download the zip</a> and drag Shot into Applications.</p>
        <ForMacs />
        <p>Shot isn't notarized by Apple yet, so macOS blocks it the first time:</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Open Shot from Applications. macOS says it can't verify Shot. Click <b>Done</b>.</li>
          <li>Open <b>System Settings</b>, go to <b>Privacy &amp; Security</b> and scroll down to Security.</li>
          <li>Click <b>Open Anyway</b> next to the message about Shot, then confirm.</li>
          <li>In Shot's welcome window, click <b>Grant</b>, turn Shot on under Screen &amp; System Audio Recording, then click <b>Relaunch</b>.</li>
          <li>Press <kbd class="key">⌘</kbd><kbd class="key">⇧</kbd><kbd class="key">4</kbd> and drag out an area.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The <a href="/docs/#first-launch">guide</a> covers the rest of the first launch.</p>
      </div>
      <Image src={openAnyway} alt="The Security section of Privacy & Security, with the Open Anyway button circled next to the message that Shot was blocked" widths={[495, 990]} sizes={half} class="shot" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px); }
  .hero .wrap { justify-items: start; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.18em; }
  .hero h1 .key { font-size: 0.62em; padding: 0.05em 0.3em; border-width: 3px; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink); }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 22px); margin: 0; max-width: 30em; }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; align-items: center; width: 100%; }
  .cta :global(.copy) { flex: 0 1 460px; min-width: 0; }
  .button.big { min-height: 52px; padding: 12px 22px; font-size: 18px; }
  .meta { margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .hero :global(.window) { width: 100%; }

  section { padding-block: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  .say { font: 800 clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px)/1.3 var(--display); letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0; max-width: 30em; text-wrap: pretty; }
  /* A tight line height keeps the caps from making a caption's line taller than plain text. */
  .say .key { font-size: 0.75em; line-height: 1.1; }
  .say .key + .key { margin-left: 0.2em; }

  .pair { display: grid; gap: 40px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; } }
  .pair > * { min-width: 0; display: grid; gap: 20px; align-content: start; }

  .narrow-text p { max-width: 36em; }
  .small p { font-size: 19px; margin: 0; }
  .small a, .install a { font-weight: 700; }

  .install h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 38px); }
  .install p { margin: 0; }
  .install .steps { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4em; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .install :global(.shot) { border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 10px; }
</style>
